#
# BENCH BUILDS ONLY: never for a release (the release job refuses a build
# with any of these options on). An overlay on sdkconfig.defaults for
# bring-up of the receiver flasher on a bench unit:
#
#   idf.py -B build-bench -D SDKCONFIG=build-bench/sdkconfig \
#          -D "SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS=sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.bench" build
#
# It adds the bench console on the UART0 console (115200, beside the log;
# every receiver byte captured), with the receiver link's bench hooks (RX
# stalls, frame timing, the loader prompt detector in report-only mode),
# and builds the receiver flasher in. The boot-time recovery of an
# interrupted update stays report-only (it logs what it would send) until
# the journal-state bench test passes; then add
# CONFIG_UM98X_FLASH_RECOVERY_ACTIONS=y for its second half. The 115200
# entry fallback stays off until its own bench test passes; cross-layout
# packages are on (UM980 11833 to 23980 tested).
#
# It also holds the receiver's first configuration until the user confirms
# it (as sdkconfig.hold): a device whose profile was never applied and whose
# automatic configuration (gnss/autocfg) was never set (saving the receiver
# page sets it) gets gnss/autocfg = 0, gnss/recovery = 2 (if unset) and
# gnss/hold = 1 before anything reaches the receiver, and only queries are
# sent until the user applies on the receiver page.
#
# With the bench console on, test-Onocoy caster slots are allowed
# (CONFIG_NTRIP_TEST_ONOCOY_SLOT, default y): a slot marked test_onocoy
# behaves as an Onocoy slot at any host, so a local test caster on this
# network sees the Onocoy retry profile and login guard without a DNS
# override.
#
# And it copies the console to the built-in USB
# (CONFIG_DIAG_CONSOLE_USB_MIRROR), so the ESP32S3 port shows the log with
# the plug either way round. That keeps the USB PHY powered while Wi-Fi runs,
# which the ESP-IDF help says can lower Wi-Fi performance (not measured on
# the station board yet). Where Wi-Fi is weak, build without it: in a new
# build directory, with an overlay after this one that says
# CONFIG_DIAG_CONSOLE_USB_MIRROR=n; in one that had the copy on, with these
# three in its sdkconfig (it keeps the other two on otherwise):
#   CONFIG_DIAG_CONSOLE_USB_MIRROR=n
#   CONFIG_USJ_ENABLE_USB_SERIAL_JTAG=n
#   CONFIG_ESP_PHY_ENABLE_USB=n

CONFIG_BENCH_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_UM98X_FLASH_ENABLE=y
CONFIG_STATION_HOLD_FIRST_APPLY=y
CONFIG_DIAG_CONSOLE_USB_MIRROR=y
